LumOn - Phase 23.8.X - WorldCell + TraceSceneRegionScheduler

Goal
- [ ] Replace TraceScene’s ad-hoc region queues with a scheduler that provides: dedup by construction, in-place priority updates, backoff/cooldowns for missing chunks, and stable convergence.
- [ ] Introduce a reusable `IWorldCell`/`WorldCell` abstraction for “sub-partitions of world space”, enabling later reuse by LumonScene surface-cache scheduling.

Non-goals (initial)
- [ ] Rewrite LumonScene surface-cache scheduling to fully use `WorldCell` (defer until TraceScene scheduler is proven).
- [ ] Achieve UE5 Lumen parity (this is scheduling + robustness work).


Phase 1 - WorldCell Primitives (Contracts + Types)
- [x] Define `WorldCellKind` enum (TraceSceneRegion, LumonSceneNear/Far, etc.).
- [x] Define `WorldCellKey` (packed `ulong` + kind encoding; allow using `ChunkKey.Packed` for TraceSceneRegion).
- [x] Define `WorldCellPriorityContext` (camera/anchor/window, frame tick, loadedness hints).
- [x] Define `IWorldCell` contract:
  - [x] `Key`, `Kind`, `Priority`, `NextEligibleTick`
  - [x] `CalculatePriority(ctx)` (pure/cheap)
  - [x] versioning fields (`CurrentVersion`, `AppliedVersion`) for staleness detection
- [x] Add base `WorldCell` type with common scheduling fields (heap index, cooldown bookkeeping).
- [x] Add unit tests for key packing/equality + basic priority contract expectations.


Phase 2 - Indexed Priority Queue (No Duplicates, O(logN) Updates)
- [x] Implement `IndexedMaxHeap<TKey>` (or `IndexedPriorityQueue<TKey>`) with:
  - [x] `Upsert(key, priority)`
  - [x] `UpdatePriority(key, priority)`
  - [x] `Remove(key)`
  - [x] `TryPopMax(out key)`
  - [x] O(1) key→heapIndex mapping (stored on entry or in a dictionary)
- [x] Unit tests:
  - [x] insert/pop ordering
  - [x] increase/decrease key updates
  - [x] remove arbitrary key
  - [x] “Upsert does not duplicate”


Phase 3 - TraceSceneRegionCell (WorldCell Specialization)
- [x] Implement `TraceSceneRegionCell : WorldCell` (or `WorldCell` + per-kind payload) with:
  - [x] `ChunkKey` / region coord (chunk units)
  - [x] `MissingStreak`, `LastSeenLoadedTick`, `LastAttemptTick`
  - [x] `CurrentVersion`, `AppliedVersion`, `InFlightVersion`
  - [x] reason flags for priority composition (distance/stale/loaded/missing)
- [x] Define TraceScene priority function terms and constants:
  - [x] distance term (camera or clipmap-anchor based)
  - [x] staleness term (never applied / applied != current)
  - [x] loadedness bonus (recently seen loaded)
  - [x] missing penalty + cooldown gate
- [x] Unit tests for priority ordering across a small synthetic window.


Phase 4 - TraceSceneRegionScheduler (Core Scheduling)
- [x] Create `TraceSceneRegionScheduler` owning:
  - [x] cell dictionary (authoritative entry per region)
  - [x] indexed heap of eligible cells
  - [x] window bounds + incremental window seeding cursor
  - [x] in-flight tracking and completion processing
  - [x] cooldown/backoff computation for `ChunkUnavailable` / snapshot unavailable
- [x] Provide public API (initial sketch):
  - [x] `SetWindow(min,max)`
  - [x] `NotifyChunkDirty(chunkKey, reason)` (optional, internal to TraceScene renderer)
  - [x] `NotifyChunkSeenLoaded(chunkKey)` (optional)
  - [x] `RefreshPriorities(ctx, budget)` (incremental or lazy)
  - [x] `TryDequeueNextEligible(nowTick, out key)` / `DequeueBatch(...)`
  - [x] `OnRequestIssued(key, version)` / `OnRequestCompleted(key, status)`
- [x] Add fairness guarantees:
  - [x] ensure “near window” cells can’t be permanently starved by far cells
  - [x] ensure cooldown-suppressed cells don’t block other work


Phase 5 - Wire Scheduler Into `LumonSceneOccupancyClipmapUpdateRenderer`
- [ ] Replace:
  - [ ] `pendingRegionsHigh/Low`, `pendingRegionKeys`
  - [ ] `maintenanceCursor`, `windowSeedCursor`, `windowSeedTotal`
  - [ ] ad-hoc re-enqueue on failure
- [ ] Drive scheduling from budgets:
  - [ ] keep `ClipmapIssueBudgetMs` / `ClipmapDispatchBudgetMs`
  - [ ] use `ClipmapMaxInFlightRegions` as the hard cap
  - [ ] keep `ClipmapMaxRegionUploadsPerFrame` / `ClipmapMaxRegionsDispatchedPerFrame` as GPU safety limits
- [ ] Ensure TraceScene only reacts to engine `ChunkDirty` via its own subscription (no LumOnModSystem invalidation).
- [ ] Add a small “loadedness hint” path using observed chunk events (inside TraceScene renderer).


Phase 6 - Backoff/Cooldown Policy (Convergence Under Missing Chunks)
- [ ] Implement exponential backoff for `ChunkUnavailable` with clamp (e.g. up to 5s).
- [ ] Add “never retry faster than X ms” to prevent per-frame churn.
- [ ] Add “seen loaded recently” override to re-enable quickly when chunk arrives.
- [ ] Unit tests:
  - [ ] missing chunk does not dominate dequeue results
  - [ ] once chunk becomes available, it regains priority and is scheduled promptly


Phase 7 - Metrics + Debugging Hooks
- [ ] Add scheduler metrics:
  - [ ] eligible heap size
  - [ ] suppressed (cooldown) count
  - [ ] in-flight count
  - [ ] applied count
  - [ ] completion breakdown (success/unavailable/canceled/superseded/failed)
  - [ ] cooldown skips
- [ ] Extend TS overlay string to include scheduler counters (top-k + reason bits).
- [ ] Add optional debug “dump scheduler state” log button (top N entries with reason).


Phase 8 - Extend WorldCell For LumonScene (Design-only Follow-up)
- [ ] Define `LumonSceneRegionCell : WorldCell` responsibilities (near/far membership + residency/capture/relight summary).
- [ ] Define how chunkSlot + generation + atlas residency map into the cell.
- [ ] Identify which existing LumonScene systems become “cell processors” later:
  - [ ] PatchId feedback → capture queue
  - [ ] Relight queue
  - [ ] Eviction / residency safety rules

